Changes Explained
Support for PCM Audio Format:
Added PCM as a supported audio format specifically for iOS clients
PCM format works better with iOS AudioQueue Services as it can be fed directly to the audio hardware
Client Type Detection:
Added a new clientType parameter to identify iOS clients
This allows special handling for iOS without breaking existing clients
Sample Rate Specification:
Added a sampleRate parameter so iOS clients can specify what they need
Default is 24000 Hz which matches XTTS v2 output
iOS-Optimized Streaming Parameters:
Smaller chunk sizes for iOS clients to reduce initial latency
Still maintains sufficient overlap for seamless playback
Audio Format Metadata:
Sends format metadata JSON message for iOS clients
Helps iOS app configure AudioQueue correctly before receiving audio data
Chunk Size Header:
Added a 4-byte header before each PCM chunk
Contains the byte size of the following chunk
Allows iOS to properly allocate buffer sizes for each chunk
Special Termination Signal:
Sends a zero-size header to signal stream completion
Helps iOS app know when playback should end
These changes enable iOS clients to use AudioQueue Services while maintaining backward compatibility with all existing clients and the current API.